+
+Read README, run `spikes/gfx-03-backend-bakeoff/repro.ps1 -Mode code` from this exact isolated worktree, then `-Mode seal` to verify final bytes. Branch `feature/gfx-03-2026-10-09`, base `17b1db4201a28e7b607c30707bdc2b75e3484a10`. The candidate is uncommitted. No Plannotator/commit/push authority was exercised.
+
+## Consume small ports
+
+- `src/materials.ts`: WebGL hook + TSL material/sky functions preserve actual fixed-base HVP strata/ripple/Fresnel/glint/sky and existing wet/wind formulas. Imported original sources/tests remain byte-identical at the two bound commits.
+- `src/port.ts`: verified RT mesh/camera/material/source copies, stable owner-local wind, immutable metadata plus borrowed depth/camera matrices. Native depth convention differs by backend; do not assume identical clip range. Invalidate borrowed texture inputs on host epoch changes; host retains renderer/session/source authority.
+- `src/run-profile.mjs`: finite functional/negative/loss/resize profile; `repro-profile.json` gives actual commands and the runner remainder. No second PresentationSession, Temporal engine or upscaler implementation is provided.
+
+Implementation/code/functionality COMPLETE/PASS is separate from strict visual parity FAIL. Adoption REQUIRES_DECISION; product integration NO; hardware/reference/performance/human visual acceptance NOT_RUN. Source provenance remains eight ANALYTICAL plus one RD_SYNTHETIC, zero PRODUCT_EXPORT. Native shadows are executed but not declared pixel-equivalent. The bounded optical candidate is one layer, not full volume integration. Historical RAY02/RAY03 and ROI shortcomings remain unchanged.
+
+The final profile is own Spec `tests/browser-profile-review-corrections-v1.json`, 169 PASS checks and 55 unique source shaders. Twelve screenshot/JSON pairs include three water undersides. Emission, depth/side faults, loss invalidation and observed shadow-target disposal are exercised. Source/RT manifests, lock, emitted dist, dependencies including unused transitive WASM, tools, ignored evidence and full Git dirty/index bytes are sealed. Raw failures remain available. MCP browser evaluations have result/status rather than invented process exit codes; CLI evidence validation records its real exit separately.
+
+Only the active A0 integrator in STATE may bind/adopt this into current HVP/Stage1-G03/G04. No native/GPU/HVP pilot or reference run is authorized by this handoff. Obtain the serial A0 slot for real closure, dedicated adapter identity, quality-fixed compile/upload/GPU/frame costs, and human water/volume/material assessment. Do not change Golden thresholds or product dependency/bootstraps here. All handoff delivery remains through the orchestrator.
+
+Human review must include untracked files and ignored evidence, not just `git diff`. `binding-manifest.json` is the exact file/index/build/dependency inventory, with digest in receipt. A0 must obtain genuine human Plannotator approval for its exact final integrated diff before commit or first push. This handoff does not grant such approval.
