+# Native ray follow-up — executable native comparison, fidelity/cost gates remain
+
+PRODUCT_INTEGRATED=false; ART=PENDING_OWNER. Historical original 0/6 and separate supplement 2/4 remain immutable, and the historical candidate remains REJECT for that exact version. New candidate evidence is not pooled with them.
+
+## Fresh original failure
+
+`runs/ray-original-red-01/report.json` reproduces the exact original package's visible F00 path in pinned Chromium/Playwright. The actual driver fragment shader contains `uvec4 sample=sourceCell(cell)` and rejects the reserved identifier. Shader/source bytes and native compiler/link facts are captured, not a string-only or CPU-DDA substitute. No linked native draw succeeds; the view is hidden and terminal. The original shader failure follows actual native allocations; no global zero-allocation-before-compiler guarantee is claimed.
+
+The observation also records four fallback textures and three scratch framebuffers remaining after program/buffer/VAO deletion. Inspection of pinned Three 0.185.1 confirms that WebGLState constructs the four fallback textures, WebGLRenderer constructs three scratch FBOs, and renderer.dispose does not delete them. These are per-renderer constructor objects, separate from the ray's CPU projection objects, source textures and numeric probe allocations. A new ordinary full-dispose and post-fault population must verify their actual final ownership.
+
+## One bounded repair round
+
+Only the local GLSL identifier and its four uses become `cellValue`; DDA stepping, boundaries/ties, normals, material selection, depth and visibility semantics are unchanged. The shared kernel remains used verbatim by actual visible and numeric passes.
+
+The freshly observed lifecycle defect authorizes the small local RD13 index.ts repair: capture returned texture/FBO handles only during createThreeLabHost's synchronous renderer construction, restore both native factory property descriptors before async source build/first draw, and delete only captured constructor handles after normal/error/abort disposal. Payload uploads remain normal effect-owned Three resources. The direct factory Abort regression below repairs the same outer disposal route within this bounded cleanup round. No shared host/dependency/global config edit, context loss, engine rebuild or new rendering path.
+
+Fresh run `ray-candidate-native-01`, build `candidate-original-02`, actually executes the visible F00 kernel, successful driver compile/link and linked-program draws. Shared numeric kernel SHA256 `475cb2fa221c13007566d76d013b312eae19ddc63063942170b7b043c9520060`. Sources/build bytes are bound in `runs/candidate-original-02-build.json`; source state is UNCOMMITTED_HASH_BOUND pending the separate exact-diff commit gate.
+
+The recorded adapted helper population is **11/12 PASS,1FAIL, exit1**, not a green overall suite. Independent review found that its RAY03 body omitted the original positive-distance and Source-ID/Owner assertions. Its saved expected result is a miss without t: the unchanged original positive-distance assertion would FAIL. The former original5/6 interpretation was incorrect and is withdrawn. The raw11/12 file remains unchanged.
+
+Fresh final build `candidate-original-04` binds all83 source/package files and the report-local direct-Abort test input in `runs/candidate-original-04-build.json`. The unchanged `tests/RD-13/native.spec.ts` actually runs under pinned Playwright: **4/6 PASS,2FAIL, exit1**, `runs/ray-original-assertions-01/report.json`. RAY02 fails on absent removed source cell at original tick90; RAY03 fails its original positive-distance assertion with undefined t. RAY01, RAY04, normal controls and selected F01 pass. No original test/input/threshold is changed.
+
+The corrected helper `ray-candidate-native-02` has **10/12 PASS,2FAIL, exit1**, independently preserving those two original negatives with the missing assertions restored. Its six supplemental visible/source-corrected/cleanup bodies pass. RAY01 contains12/12 real numeric cases and five intentionally faulty readbacks all correctly rejected, separate from both six- and twelve-body denominators. Actual360 source edit/stale/depth and actual360→720 transform/occupied-voxel positive-distance/source retention supplements pass. Native driver/backend identity and actual submitted frames are retained in the report. These results do not pool historical0/6+2/4, adapted11/12, final original4/6 or final helper10/12.
+
+Ordinary complete disposal and actual post-allocation fragment compiler/link failures all pass in the final helper: terminal/hidden view, no old READY/frame, idempotent repeated dispose and explicit remount recovery. The faults alter actual shader source or detach an actual fragment shader before linking; no native result is faked. All observed created handles (buffers/textures/programs/shaders/FBOs/VAOs/renderbuffers/queries/samplers/transform-feedback) return0 before page close. Captured constructor arrays clear after base cleanup; source/format admission still precedes large payload projection, while valid native compilation legitimately allocates resources. Physical driver/VRAM reclamation remains unsupported.
+
+## Direct factory Abort regression
+
+The normal UI's mountExperiment wrapper already disposed the outer handle, so it masked the direct factory route. Report-local native-abort.html calls the unchanged actual factory interface directly. `ray-abort-red-02` reproduces the visible ready-host defect on candidate-abort-red-03: abort leaves terminal.disposed=false and the canvas visible even though the base host is aborted. Before-init and during-init controls pass separately. The preceding ray-abort-red-01 failed Chromium spawn with sandbox EPERM before native execution and remains an invocation log, not a native RED.
+
+The small fix sends Abort through the returned outer dispose route, immediately hides/retires the terminal, removes its listeners and then awaits base/constructor cleanup. A signal already aborted after initialization cleans up before Terminal creation and rejects. `ray-abort-green-01` on candidate-original-04 passes **3/3, exit0**: ready direct Abort, abort during native allocation/init, and abort before init. Ready Abort records terminal.disposed=true/hidden=true synchronously, no active host diagnostics and all observed native handles0 before any explicit handle.dispose. Repeated explicit disposal leaves the same zero counts. During-init actually allocates native objects before clean rejection; before-init remains allocation-free. No outer mountExperiment cleanup is used as the proof.
+
+## Original invocation boundaries
+
+The published RAY02 invokes tick90, but the preserved F06 edit is at360: the unchanged original case freshly FAILS on the removed-cell prerequisite before its edit assertions, while the separate actual360 edit/stale/depth supplement PASSES. RAY03's ticks60/120 do not exercise the actual360/720 detach/rotation transition and its original inside input produces a miss, so its required positive distance FAILS. The source-corrected supplemental case separately proves the actual transition and source-ID retention. Its inside-volume input is computed from an actually occupied original voxel and exact owner/root transforms and produces a real positive-distance hit. Neither result is promoted beyond the input that was actually exercised.
+
+## Remaining axes
+
+The bounded ray route omits AO; selected F01 is only the admitted64-cubed source window plus original water presentation, with vegetation omitted and outside source coverage Unknown. Numeric attachment readback is not full beauty/water/sky/shadow/PBR parity.
+
+Full decoded native PNG observations at1320x743 (no resampling): F00 mean RGB error0.0000823264/max83byte; F01 mean0.000622341/max78byte; alpha is byte-exact. Neither pair is byte-exact RGBA. Actual compositor dimensions are recorded separately from drawing-buffer settings. Do not invent a new permissive threshold or assume those differences are only MSAA edges. The small global mean is not proof of identical sample coverage/AA or full image fidelity. Therefore equal-quality ray cost/winner qualification is **DEFER_NEW_SPIKE_REQUIRED** for independently sensitive raster/AA/interior/depth-water qualification; no further shader/architecture repair is attempted in this finite round.
