+# RT-08 isolated snapshot photo candidate
+
+Hypothesis: a standing immutable Hestia presentation snapshot can feed a separate progressive photo path without any live World access, simulation pause or gameplay renderer change. This is a disposable research candidate, not product integration.
+
+Execution: **LOCAL_WINDOWS_ISOLATED**. Base `17b1db4201a28e7b607c30707bdc2b75e3484a10`, branch `feature/rt-08-2026-10-09`. Own package only. Node 22.23.2/npm 10.9.8, Python 3.12.13 inspected (not used). No Rust required. Approved DOM browser Chromium 151.0.7922.34; initial configured browser diagnostics 155 retained separately.
+
+Pins: `three@0.186.1`, `@types/three@0.186.0`, `three-gpu-pathtracer@0.0.27`, `three-mesh-bvh@0.9.16`, mandatory peer `xatlas-web@0.1.0`; TS 5.9.3, esbuild 0.28.2 and WebGPU types 0.1.64. Primary npm metadata and published integrity are in `dependency-primary.json`; installed exports, peers, licenses and complete bytes are sealed. The pathtracer/BVH peers accept this Three target, so it was not downgraded.
+
+The upstream [pathtracer source/README at its pinned npm gitHead](https://github.com/gkjohnson/three-gpu-pathtracer/tree/afc7db6294c15185752b22abc553d17168aaae9b) documents WebGPU and Standard/Physical materials. The candidate uses the actual installed `WebGPUPathTracer`, `setScene`, `renderSample`, `getSampleCountsAsync`, `reset`, `setSize`, `updateCamera` and `dispose` APIs. [BVH pinned source](https://github.com/gkjohnson/three-mesh-bvh/tree/79dd84170de5066bcadff155a2d78fd243b1b14b) provides the CPU BVH control and WebGPU BVH dependency. Both package licenses are MIT. Installed license files and transitive licenses are bound by `binding-manifest.json`; metadata is not a substitute for preserving them.
+
+From this spike directory:
+
+```powershell
+$rtNode='C:\IFI_SourceCode\Utils\npm-tmp\opencode\node-v22.23.2-win-x64\node.exe'
+& $rtNode seal.mjs --verify
+& $rtNode check.mjs inputs inputs-repro-01
+& $rtNode check.mjs control control-repro-01
+& $rtNode check.mjs typecheck typecheck-repro-01
+& $rtNode check.mjs build build-repro-01
+& $rtNode check.mjs test tests-repro-01
+& $rtNode serve.mjs
+```
+
+Evidence labels must be new; existing raw logs are never overwritten. Open the printed localhost port. Default route constructs the snapshot and DOM only; it never requests a GPU. GPU rendering requires `?runner=1` and explicit start, solely in an authorized Runner/A0 slot. `repro.ps1` verifies the frozen handoff; `--rerun` writes fresh evidence and intentionally invalidates the old full evidence seal until a newly reviewed handoff is made.
+
+For a clean reinstall use the approved Node/npm paths with `npm ci --ignore-scripts --no-audit --no-fund --cache .cache --offline=false`; no shared node_modules or package configuration is copied. Reinstall/build changes require fresh byte verification. Producer import is a one-time producer-dependent preparation; normal execution uses owned frozen bytes and never imports a moving neighbor worktree.
+
+The near camera comes from GFX03's bound port. Source provenance is **RD_SYNTHETIC_F00_CONTROL**, not a product export. Five opaque base-PBR meshes are built; foliage is omitted and marked unsupported. Water, procedural GFX strata/AO/wetness/wind/sky/ambient are unsupported and explicitly reported. Base emissive/roughness/color/double-sided properties reuse `surfaceMaterial`; pathtracer does not adopt its shader hooks. GFX03 image/version/backend parity remains **FAIL**. No equal-look, water, foliage or realtime claim follows from this candidate.
+
+Each photo binds source/geometry/material/light/camera/frame/snapshot digests plus actual capture projection/view/output size, stable-noise seed policy and PNG SHA256. Private inputs cannot be reached through the scene: rebuilding creates independent geometry buffers. Authoring replacement disposes the old photo path and requires a fresh explicit renderer/accumulation. No active world, clock, physics, settings store or simulation pause is imported.
+
+`repro-profile.json` and `runner-profile.js` define finite 32/128/512-spp runs (180 seconds / 8192 dispatches each), raw images, sample counts, own-scope output and bounded lifecycle checks. Use `node serve.mjs --runner` for the origin-checked localhost capture writer. The Runner navigates its own preview page, then uses the configured Playwright `browser_run_code_unsafe` with the profile filename. Files land only under `captures/rt08-<run-id>/`. Actual convergence/art/cost/device-loss evidence remains **NOT_RUN** here. The 512-spp image is an internal comparison endpoint, not independent ground truth; the owner must decide art quality.
