+# RT-08 result
+
+**Local finite implementation: COMPLETE. Full RT-08/hardware acceptance: PARTIAL. Code/CPU/DOM: PASS. GPU/convergence/cost/art/reference: NOT_RUN. Recommendation: REQUIRES_DECISION. Product integration: NO.**
+
+The executable candidate constructs owned static Three geometry from 151 verified copied GFX03/RT01 files. Both original producer seals verified source/index/dirty/build/dependency/tool/fixture/shader bindings before copying. Receipt/seal anchors are unchanged; destination member path, source path, length and SHA256 are listed in `input-bindings.json`. Exact task documents and the read-time RT08 management identity are in `task-bindings.json`. The live producer worktrees are not runtime imports.
+
+The fixed-base product picker and 1000 unique deterministic DDA rays against the independent exhaustive oracle pass unchanged (9/9 controls, exit 0). Candidate tests pass 20/20 (exit 0): exact input tamper detection; actual CPU scene/BVH; private buffers and disposal; six digest dimensions; malformed camera/material/indices/frames; installed API import; mock driver cancel/resize/loss/errors; async stale PNG and protected provenance; bounded artifact-storage names/integrity/overwrite negatives; post-completion Resize and never-resolving readback deadlines. Mock driver/PNG/storage results are labelled MOCK and do not prove a hardware driver or actual encoded PNG.
+
+Typecheck and production build pass (exit 0). Latest build/input proof binds the real source closure and emitted browser/CPU bundles. Actual DOM diagnostics pass on an explicitly selected existing Chromium 151.0.7922.34 binary under C:\IFI_SourceCode, tool-native, headless/multiprocess with GPU disabled. Default page never requests a GPU. Desktop, 390-pixel narrow and disposed screenshots plus full result are in the own spec tests directory. The prior configured-browser 155 run had unverified executable location; it is historical diagnosis, not the final approved executable binding.
+
+Initial failures are preserved: sandbox child-process EPERM; npm cache-only metadata errors; missing copied historical picker; expected missing lifecycle implementation RED; a geometry-test fractional mutation on Uint32 (fixed by mutating a positions Float32 payload, assertion unchanged); DOM controls left enabled after Dispose (fixed and reproduced); default preview port collision (switched to OS-assigned port); Playwright VM refused dynamic Node imports (profiles use tool-native APIs and a bounded own-scope HTTP writer). Failed raw outputs were not overwritten. No numerical tolerance or historical oracle was weakened.
+
+Actual capture API uses measured minimum per-pixel samples, stableNoise reset, fresh geometry/camera resources and epoch checks before adopting async readbacks/PNG. Scene replacement rebuilds from a new digest and disposes prior resources. Cancel/resize invalidate immediately; normal cleanup waits for outstanding readbacks. A separate wall deadline and terminal AbortSignal prevent a never-resolving readback from holding owned resources indefinitely; Dispose/loss interrupts the waiting wrapper and destroys the owned device before resource release. Resize re-enables the UI after its queue settles. These two independent reviewer findings have focused regressions. The Runner's finally path invokes cleanup. Device-loss model tests are unit diagnostics; the finite runner includes an injected disposal/loss check, which must not be called actual involuntary driver loss. Missing GPU timers are `UNSUPPORTED_NOT_INSTRUMENTED`, not 0. CPU dispatch/readback and wall duration include stalls/readbacks and are not exact GPU pass times. Runner server startup verifies the complete code seal; photo sidecars include code/lock/input/shader-source-list digests and reject backend/device identity drift. Actual compiled GPU shaders still require Runner instrumentation.
+
+Unsupported profiles: water, foliage and GFX custom shaders/ambient/sky. Omitted leaves are visible in the metadata. This retains five opaque base-PBR meshes with direct sunlight. The source snapshot is RD synthetic and uses GFX03's near camera. The original GFX03 version/backend pixel parity fails 3/3 + 3/3 and stays FAIL; prior RD original Rays 4/6 (RAY02/RAY03 FAIL) versus corrected-helper 10/12 remain separate historical populations. None was rerun or requalified by this photo spike.
+
+No GPU, native, HVP, 42/1400 series or performance benchmark ran. No qualified device/resource window existed. GPU sample/convergence images, spp costs, exact compiled WGSL, hardware loss, cross-device and human art review are NOT_RUN. All shader source bytes, dependency WASMs (unused xatlas peer/types Rapier, not PHY migration) and full source/index/evidence/build/dependency/tool bindings accompany the handoff. Rapier 0.21 product migration remains A0/PHY scope; unused transitive Rapier is not that migration.
+
+DevToolbox `verify_run` passed spec validation (exit 0) but its inherited root `.devtoolbox/verify.json` attempted a product full typecheck (exit 1, missing `apps/weltraum-browser/node_modules/typescript/bin/tsc`). That preset is outside the exclusive task's write scope; the own spike typecheck/build pass. No shared product dependencies or foreign verification config were repaired. Completion preflight is recorded honestly and spec tasks remain open if that gate blocks them; this is not a failing RT08 typecheck disguised as PASS.
+
+Browser tooling incident: the verifier's configured runtime automatically created five page/console files in the main checkout `.playwright-mcp`. They are preserved and listed/digested in the handoff/seal; no product/spec/package/lock bytes there were changed by RT08. Root must account for them. No configuration, plugin, daemon or service was repaired. No commit, push, merge, publication or Plannotator approval was performed.
